This is a status update to my patch ("color-ls") for GNU ls that
provides filename colorization, 8-bit (ISO 8859) support and
ls/dir/vdir unified to a single binary.

It was originally developed within the Linux community but works on
(just about) any machine that uses GNU ls.  Filename colorization and
8-bit support is dependent on OS and terminal support, of course.

	----

GNU fileutils, which includes GNU ls, version 3.9 was recently
released.  The color-ls patch for GNU fileutils 3.8.4f works
unmodified with GNU fileutils 3.9, if the following patching
instructions are used:

Get color-ls-3.8.4f.patch.gz and fileutils-3.9.tar.gz.
Execute the following commands:

	zcat fileutils-3.9.tar.gz | tar xvf -
	cd fileutils-3.9
	zcat ../color-ls-3.8.4f.patch.gz | patch -p1

Then follow the instructions in the INSTALL file as usual.

color-ls-3.8.4f.patch.gz is available on sunsite.unc.edu:
	/pub/Linux/utils/file/color-ls-3.8.4f.patch.gz

fileutils-3.9.tar.gz is available on prep.ai.mit.edu:
	/pub/gnu/fileutils-3.9.tar.gz

An updated LSM entry follows.

