Sorry about the frequency of releases, but it seems like the only time
people ask me to implement a new feature is when I have just released
a new version.  Hence there is a new color-ls patch for GNU fileutils
3.9; this one adds a --color-if-tty option, suitable for sticking in a
command alias if your pager or other program doesn't support color
codes.

The color-ls patch implements code to colorize files listings
depending on type, adds support for 8-bit ISO-8859 characters and
unifies ls, dir, and vdir to a single binary.

	/hpa

