Announcing QUOTA-1.1. Diskquotas for Linux and ACCOUNTING 1.0
process accounting for Linux

I finally can announce the second and much improved release of
diskquotas for the LINUX O.S. This release makes the quota-1.0
package obsolete. For people going from the 1.0 release to the
1.1 release, don't panic the quotafile structure hasn't changed
and is still compatible with the BSD quotasystem.

The utils included in the package are mostly ported commands from BSD
sources with some modifications by me because of little differences
between BSD and LINUX. The only thing we had to make redo was
the quotacheck program. Because the BSD quota stuff is only usable for
ufs-filesystems we had to write that one from scratch. This one is a
user-level one that doesn't use raw-device info but readdir to walk
trough the filesystem-tree. It seem to be quite fast even on IDE-disks.

In this new release there is also included a rquota program to query
for quota on linux-machines from which you mount your disks. I wrote
this from scratch and so don't know if it compatible with the other
implementations floating arround. The main difference is that we have
two kind of quota so I hacked the rquota.x file to allow us to use
those two kinds of quota.

The package contains :
	- kernel diffs for 0.99pl13 source tree
	  (Please read the file README.FIRST on how to install !)
	  These diffs also contain some code to make accounting
	  of processes possible but that is still very limited but
	  somewhat useful. (You need the acct-1.0 package to make use
	  of the accounting stuff)
	  (The diffs are in because it didn't want to edit the diffs
	   any more as I already did. And quota and accounting aren't
	   that much apart).
	- quotaon/quotaoff program (ported from BSD)
	- edquota program (ported from BSD)
	- repquota program (ported from BSD)
	- quota program (ported from BSD) (Can query remote machines
                                           for quota for NFS mounted
                                           disks)
	- quotacheck program (new one, faster about 60%)
	- rquota programs
	- some diffs for strace2 to trace calls to quotactl.
	- Fixed some caveats that were in the previous
	  release, with allocating quota when there isn't
	  enough quota.

I probably forgot something but if you want more info read the files
README.FIRST and Changelog.

