A new version of my eps dvi driver for epson-like printers is
available.  This is eps03.tgz (gzip compressed tar file).  This new
version is highly configurable, and should work with many kinds of
printers.  

This software is provided in source form.  To build this you need a
c++ compiler, and you will need bison and flex (from FSF).

As shipped this will build on linux and other unixes.  It will
probably need minor modification to use lex and yacc instead of flex
and bison.

An earlier version worked on msdos using djgpp.  I haven't tried this
on the current version.

An earlier version worked on borland c++, but needs to use a 2-pass
approach to reduce the bitmap size.  The current version of eps does
currently support this, but it should be quite easy to put it back.  I
don't use msdos anymore, so if you are interested you can probably do
this yourself.

eps03.tgz is available at sunsite.unc.edu, and at ftp.ctd.comsat.com.

